<BaseLayout title={title} description={desc} site={site} path={path}>
  <ArticleSchema title={title} description={desc} siteName={site.name} domain={site.domain} path={path} />
  <section class="py-16 md:py-24 container">
    <a href="/alternatives" class="link text-sm font-bold">← All alternatives</a>
    <h1 class="hero-title mt-6">Best Justuno alternatives for cart recovery</h1>
    <p class="mt-6 max-w-3xl text-xl text-slate-700">Migration playbook when Justuno no longer fits margin-safe recovery on Shopify.</p>
    <div class="mt-10">
      <TldrBox title="Ranked alternatives" picks={[{ label: '#1', tool: 'Sequenzy', reason: 'Lifecycle layer and playbook-first cart recovery.' }, { label: '#2', tool: alt2.name, reason: 'Shopify depth and multichannel.' }, { label: 'Leaving', tool: leaving.name, reason: leaving.tagline }]} />
    </div>
    <div class="prose-shopify mt-10">
      <p>All numbered scenarios and deep dives below are synthetic illustrations, not observed merchant results, distinct researched incidents, or timing guarantees. Contribution holds product cost fixed at AOV × (1 − margin): discounted contribution is AOV × (margin − discount), and the loss is AOV × discount. Fees, returns, shipping and incremental recovery are excluded. Proposed touch timings, caps and purchase exits require validation in the actual sending system; a documented opt-in label alone does not establish permission for every purpose or jurisdiction.</p>
      <p>Justuno combines onsite capture with connected workflows. Its <a class="link" href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/425-workflows-in-justuno">workflow documentation</a> describes syncing captured data to other apps; its <a class="link" href="https://hub.justuno.com/article/1054-visitor-id-resolution-identify">Visitor ID documentation</a> places follow-up email triggers in the connected ESP/CRM. Inventory the actual capture form, profile identity, destination list, event mapping and sender before changing tools. Check downstream purchase state, purpose-specific permission, replay deduplication and suppressions at send time; assign an owner for messages already queued in each system.</p>
